# Runexis numbers

The handbook is the live page `https://didapi.runexis.ru/docs/index.html`. Read it again before any Runexis change. It can change. Do not invent methods, paths, or query fields. Do not commit a copy of that page.

The host is the literal `https://didapi.runexis.ru`. HTTPS only. Do not follow redirects. Do not trust a custom certificate. Timeout 30s. Body cap 20 MB.

This release may send only:

- `POST /api/v1/login` with `email` and `password`, once at the start of a walk and once for the access check. It issues a Bearer token and a refresh token. It does not change numbers.
- `POST /api/v1/refresh` with body exactly `{token}` equal to the refresh token, once after a catalog read returns 401, then that same GET once. A 403 does not refresh. Refresh is not used on login.
- `GET /api/v1/numbers/management` with `page` and `limit=30` only. A row is purchased only when `status.mnemonic` is present and is not `free`. A missing status fails the page. A `free` row is counted and is not staged.
- `GET /api/v1/regions/codes` once after the partner list is complete, and once in the access check after that first partner page. The body is a directory of `city_id` and three-digit `codes`. City names and region names are not stored. An empty directory, a body that is not `success: true`, or a code that is not three digits publishes nothing.
- `GET /api/v1/numbers/showcase` with `page`, `limit=30`, and `region_codes[0][]` set to one three-digit code taken from that directory row. `city_ids[]` is added only when that same row has an integer `city_id`. One code is one request, even when the row lists several codes. The whole page is the free draft.

No unfiltered showcase. No `class_id`, `phone_number`, or `number_status_id`. The values are not taken from a caller, a flag, or a saved catalog. The load reads every management page first. A failed purchased list does not open the code directory or the showcase. Completeness is that code's `meta.total`. A short page ends that code only when the accepted count equals that total. A hole, a changed total, or a failed page publishes nothing. The same `e164` on a later code is skipped by the draft key and the walk continues. The same `e164` twice on one page fails that page. Both catalogs are replaced only after every code succeeds. The access check reads page 1 of management, then the code directory, then page 1 of the showcase for the first code of the first directory row. A page that cannot be parsed is not access. The password, the token, and the refresh token stay out of logs, the database, and responses.

Do not call `revoke-all`, `buy`, `book`, `allocate`, `refuse`, `GET /api/v1/numbers`, `GET /api/v1/internal/numbers`, `GET /api/v1/regions`, or `GET /api/v1/regions/cities`. Do not call the old Numbering API.

A successful walk replaces every `free_numbers` row and every `purchased_numbers` row whose provider is `Runexis`, in one transaction. SipOut rows stay. Free-number prices may fill «Покупка (входящая)» and «Абонплата (входящая)». Purchased money columns stay empty. Category and class are not stored. The Runexis lease and draft are their own tables. Do not use `numbering_sync_state` or `numbering_sync_stage`. The stage log names the code, the page, the HTTP status, the attempts, and the duration. It is synced at the end of a code and on failure. It has no password, token, or URL.
